# Minitest and Test::Unit run every public `test_` method of a test case
# by its name, which no call site writes, so a test was `unreferenced`,
# clear: deleting it fails nothing. In a class `--dead` already calls a test
# case (in a test directory, inheriting one or in a file named as a test),
# such a method is `convention-only`, by the test runner. A private one is
# not run, a class in a test directory that is no test case runs nothing,
# and neither does a `test_` method in the library.
dead test WidgetTest#test_builds=convention-only WidgetTest#unused_helper=unreferenced WidgetTest#test_hidden=unreferenced FakeClock#test_mode=unreferenced ClockCase#test_ticks=convention-only
dead lib Widget#test_connection=unreferenced
